WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.362 --> 00:00:01.570
SPEAKER: What's up, everyone?

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:04.070
Thanks for checking out "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.700
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.367
Navigating the
Cloud can be tricky.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.450
So we want to make sure
you have all the tools you

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.800
need to succeed.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.500
First up, we're hosting an
instructor-led training session

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.450
to help you get the
fundamentals together.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.650
This class will
give you an overview

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.733
of some of the most popular
Google Cloud solutions

00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:21.720
through presentations,
demos, and hands-on labs.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.340
Come learn with us.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.080
Of course, if you're not in
the area or you can't make it,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.413
you can also check out the
fundamentals or other courses

00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:28.950
on Coursera.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:30.960
This is a great tool
for self-paced learning,

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.700
and you still get a
try running the code

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.105
with hands-on tutorials.

00:00:34.105 --> 00:00:36.480
There are tons of courses that
can help you learn and get

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.170
certified.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.520
So find the right
content for you.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.290
Now, once you know
the fundamentals,

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.748
you'll probably want to try
running some jobs in the Cloud.

00:00:43.748 --> 00:00:45.630
Google Cloud Composer
is a managed version

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.610
of Apache Airflow
that automatically

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.477
scales to run your workflows.

00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:51.060
We've just launched
a solution article

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.685
to help you get a
better understanding,

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.020
run a sample workflow that
backs up virtual machines,

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:58.080
and it gets you ready to start
customizing your own jobs.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.490
Try it out for yourself
and see what you can build.

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.490
Now, again, if what you're
trying to build needs

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:05.088
security-- and spoiler
alert, it probably does--

00:01:05.088 --> 00:01:07.380
and you want to manage the
cryptographic keys yourself,

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.840
there are also some new client
libraries and code samples

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.300
for you to get started from.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.050
The Cloud Key Management
Service gives you

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.420
control of your encryption
and integrates into our Cloud

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.370
Identity suite, letting
you more easily build

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:18.763
secure applications.

00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:21.180
Check out the new samples and
use the new client libraries

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.890
to secure your apps.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.840
And if your apps
use speech-to-text

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.910
or text-to-speech,
we're excited to share

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.700
that we've rolled out some great
updates, more features, more

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.063
voices, more languages, better
accuracy, and lower prices.

00:01:33.063 --> 00:01:34.980
If you've been interested
in trying these out,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.480
there's no better time than now.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.490
So check out how we've
made our models better,

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.387
then try them out for yourself.

00:01:40.387 --> 00:01:41.970
And don't forget,
the first 60 minutes

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.732
of audio you process every month
with speech-to-text is free.

00:01:44.732 --> 00:01:46.815
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:49.590
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:50.760
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.540
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.553
We'll see you in the Cloud.

